{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QXJovr9g6mARVf8rStSuqw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Spec: issue 2, splitting a damage charge loses a cent\n2\t\n3\t## Outcome\n4\t\n5\tWhen a damage charge does not divide evenly between borrowers, every penny is still billed to someone.\n6\tSplitting £33.33 (3333 cents) two ways gives £16.67 and £16.66, which add up to £33.33.\n7\t\n8\t## Requirements\n9\t\n10\t- The system shall return shares that add up to exactly the charge in cents.\n11\t- When the charge does not divide evenly, the system shall give the leftover cents to the first borrowers, one cent each, so 3333 split 2 ways is [1667, 1666].\n12\t- The system shall keep every share within one cent of every other share.\n13\t- When the charge divides evenly, the system shall give every borrower the same share.\n14\t- If the charge is not a whole number of cents or is negative, then the system shall refuse it with an error.\n15\t- If the number of ways is not a whole number or is less than 1, then the system shall refuse it with an error.\n16\t\n17\t## Must not change\n18\t\n19\t- Amounts stay integer cents; no floats.\n20\t- `splitCharge(totalCents, ways)` keeps its name, arguments and return type (an array of `ways` numbers).\n21\t- Existing tests in `tests/fees/split.test.ts` keep passing.\n22\t- Nothing under `src/auth/` changes.\n23\t\n24\t## Out of scope\n25\t\n26\t- Splitting in proportion to anything other than equal shares.\n27\t- Late fees (`src/fees/late.ts`) and the desk command's output format.\n28\t- Any change to the tests that already exist.\n29\t\n30\t## Done when\n31\t\n32\t- The new tests in `tests/fees/split.test.ts` pass.\n33\t- `bun run gate` exits 0.\n34\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8658a45-25a9-4071-a491-f956293c1dd0","uuid":"b8fb4cdb-e956-486f-8760-c2013964f756","timestamp":"2026-11-13T05:07:22.424Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/user/software-factory-claude-code/parts/06-price-and-ship/03-ship-the-factory/solution/runs/2/repo/specs/2/SPEC.md","content":"# Spec: issue 2, splitting a damage charge loses a cent\n\n## Outcome\n\nWhen a damage charge does not divide evenly between borrowers, every penny is still billed to someone.\nSplitting £33.33 (3333 cents) two ways gives £16.67 and £16.66, which add up to £33.33.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- The system shall return shares that add up to exactly the charge in cents.\n- When the charge does not divide evenly, the system shall give the leftover cents to the first borrowers, one cent each, so 3333 split 2 ways is [1667, 1666].\n- The system shall keep every share within one cent of every other share.\n- When the charge divides evenly, the system shall give every borrower the same share.\n- If the charge is not a whole number of cents or is negative, then the system shall refuse it with an error.\n- If the number of ways is not a whole number or is less than 1, then the system shall refuse it with an error.\n\n## Must not change\n\n- Amounts stay integer cents; no floats.\n- `splitCharge(totalCents, ways)` keeps its name, arguments and return type (an array of `ways` numbers).\n- Existing tests in `tests/fees/split.test.ts` keep passing.\n- Nothing under `src/auth/` changes.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Splitting in proportion to anything other than equal shares.\n- Late fees (`src/fees/late.ts`) and the desk command's output format.\n- Any change to the tests that already exist.\n\n## Done when\n\n- The new tests in `tests/fees/split.test.ts` pass.\n- `bun run gate` exits 0.\n","numLines":34,"startLine":1,"totalLines":34}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QXJovr9g6mARVf8rStSuqw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
